rotection (NUP2105L), filter caps, DNP 120R termination, hierarchical label shapes, wiring topology\",\"inputs/project/README.md feature claims cross-checked against CAN2 implementation (internal dual-wideband on CAN bus #2)\",\"work/drc/drc.json (supplied 100000-byte prefix): all schematic_parity items (114) including 15 extra_footprint and the J2 footprint substitution; silk_over_copper and lib_footprint_mismatch/lib_footprint_issues violations as included\",\"DRC check record details: violation counts by severity (error: 13) and by type (padstack 5, annular_width 5, starved_thermal 3), 0 unconnected items\",\"work/geometry/geometry.json (supplied 100000-byte prefix): pad-level net assignments for U21 (TJA1051T-3), U1 (f042_wideband_module), CAN2 filter caps C29/C30/C33/C34, DNP termination R36, DNP refs list, and other visible footprints\",\"work/drc/execution.json, work/drc/console.log, work/geometry/execution.json, work/geometry/console.log: tool invocation integrity, exit codes, hash consistency with board_sha256\"],\"limitations\":[\"ERC and netlist checks never executed (missing sheet file 'VR Conditioner.kicad_sch'); electrical-rule and full connectivity-vs-schematic coverage is absent for the whole hierarchy\",\"work/drc/drc.json truncated at 100000/141827 bytes: the 13 error-severity violation items (padstack, annular_width, starved_thermal) fall outside the supplied prefix, so their board locations could not be inspected\",\"work/geometry/geometry.json truncated at 100000/1657568 bytes: track segments (2207), vias (1224), and zones (18) were not supplied; no clearance, return-path, or current-path geometry review was possible\",\"No stackup, copper weight, or thermal data supplied; ampacity and thermal qualification of high-current paths (IGBT ignition drivers, H-bridges, lowside outputs) cannot be assessed and must not be inferred from widths\",\"Only one schematic sheet (wbo-can-trans) supplied; the root sheet, VR conditioner sheet, and all other hierarchy content were not reviewable\",\"Zone fill evaluated strictly as saved (read-only candidate); starved_thermal findings reflect the saved fill state and could not be re-verified by refilling\",\"Termination state of the plug-in f042 wideband modules and of the external harness is outside the packet; the CAN2 termination finding is conditional on those unknowns\",\"Declared scope exclusions apply: no automotive transient, ignition energy, wideband control stability, EMC, or thermal qualification was performed\"],\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"F1\",\"title\":\"Hierarchy references missing sheet file 'VR Conditioner.kicad_sch' (filename case mismatch), breaking ERC/netlist and corrupting parity coverage\",\"location\":\"Project hierarchy (root references 'VR Conditioner.kicad_sch'; checkout supplies 'VR conditioner.kicad_sch'); VR conditioner section on board near (133.8, 56.1) mm\",\"condition\":\"The root schematic references a sheet filename whose case does not match the file present in the checkout. Both the ERC and netlist checks aborted as malformed ('hierarchy references missing sheet files'), and the native DRC parity pass reported exactly the VR-conditioner board components (U10 MAX9924, R25-R34, C23-C25, JP1 - 15 items) as 'Extra footprint' with no schematic counterpart.\",\"mechanism\":\"On case-sensitive filesystems the sheet cannot be loaded, so the VR conditioner circuit is absent from the compiled netlist. Schematic-to-board equivalence for the VR input section (a README-advertised feature: dual VR crank/cam inputs) is unverifiable, and any netlist-driven update or verification run would treat those footprints as orphans, risking their removal or mis-netting.\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"assessment\":\"defect\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"work/drc/drc.json\",\"locator\":\"schematic_parity: 15x type=extra_footprint (C25 uuid 0070999b, U10 uuid 4ccdf03c, R27 uuid 4f184bcb, R28 uuid 40773cef, R29 uuid 667488c6, R25, R26, R30-R34, C23, C24, JP1)\"},{\"path\":\"work/geometry/geometry.json\",\"locator\":\"footprint U10 value MAX9924 at (133.811, 56.081) with live nets (/VR1+, +5V, GND) - populated on board yet 'extra' per parity\"},{\"path\":\"work/drc/console.log\",\"locator\":\"line 3: 'Found 114 schematic parity issues'\"}],\"reasoning\":\"Two independent native tools fail on the same missing-file reference (ERC/netlist abort; DRC parity misclassifies the entire VR section), so this is a real project-data integrity defect, not a tool artifact. The affected components carry real nets in the saved board (geometry shows U10 wired to /VR1+, +5V, GND), proving the section exists physically but is invisible to native verification. Major rather than blocking because the saved copper itself reports 0 unconnected items and the defect is a one-character rename fix, but it blocks all hierarchy-level verification until corrected.\"},{\"id\":\"F2\",\"title\":\"Saved board fails native DRC with 13 error-severity violations (5 padstack, 5 annular_width, 3 starved_thermal)\",\"location\":\"Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pcb, saved copper/padstacks (specific items in truncated portion of drc.json)\",\"condition\":\"The native DRC run (kicad-cli 10.0.7, --severity-all, exit 0) reports 142 violations of which 13 are error severity. The by_type breakdown in the check record (padstack 5, annular_width 5, starved_thermal 3) sums exactly to the 13 errors.\",\"mechanism\":\"Annular-width errors mean drilled holes whose remaining copper ring is below the board minimum, risking drill breakout and open/intermittent connections after fabrication. Padstack errors indicate invalid pad/via stack definitions that fabricators may interpret inconsistently. Starved thermals mean pads whose saved zone fill provides fewer thermal spokes than required, risking a high-resistance or mechanically weak pad-to-plane connection on what are typically power/ground pads.\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"assessment\":\"defect\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"work/drc/console.log\",\"locator\":\"line 1: 'Found 142 violations'\"},{\"path\":\"work/drc/drc.json\",\"locator\":\"check details: by_severity error=13; by_type padstack=5, annular_width=5, starved_thermal=3 (individual items beyond supplied 100000-byte prefix)\"},{\"path\":\"work/drc/execution.json\",\"locator\":\"argv '--severity-all', exit_code 0, board Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pcb\"}],\"reasoning\":\"A successful tool exit does not mean the board passed: the console and report counts show 13 error-class rule violations in the saved artifact. These categories are manufacturing-reliability defects rather than cosmetic warnings. I cannot localize the items because the drc.json excerpt was truncated before the violations of error severity, so the exact nets/positions remain a coverage gap, but the existence and classification of the errors is directly evidenced by the native run.\"},{\"id\":\"F3\",\"title\":\"Internal dual-wideband CAN2 bus has zero populated 120R termination on the base board (both termination resistors DNP)\",\"location\":\"wbo-can-trans sheet instances (R36/R37, 120R 1206 across CAN2+/CAN2-); board R36 at (175.01, 142.13) mm and R37 at (81.62, 140.55) mm\",\"condition\":\"Both 120R termination resistors across /CAN2+ and /CAN2- are not populated: the schematic marks R36 '(dnp yes)', '(in_bom no)' with an 'n.p.' annotation (instance references R36 and R37 across the two sheet instances), and the board geometry lists R36 and R37 in dnp_refs with footprint R36 confirmed dnp:true spanning /CAN2+ to /CAN2-. The 47pF caps (C29/C30/C33/C34) on the bus are line-to-ground filters, not termination. README states both wideband O2 controllers are connected internally to CAN bus #2.\",\"mechanism\":\"A high-speed CAN bus without ~60R differential loading suffers reflections and reduced noise margin; depending on bit rate and stub lengths this ranges from elevated error frames to total arbitration failure. The internal CAN2 segment carries the two onboard f042 wideband modules (U1/U2) plus transceiver U21, so wideband lambda data - a core advertised feature - depends on this bus. As saved, correct operation relies entirely on termination located on the plug-in wideband modules or in the external harness, neither of which is evidenced anywhere in the packet.\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"assessment\":\"concern\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"inputs/project/wbo-can-trans.kicad_sch\",\"locator\":\"symbol R36 uuid d69380f9-5487-4782-9ce9-0690df62e543: value 120, (dnp yes), (in_bom no), instances R36/R37; text 'n.p.' uuid 98ed307b at (113.03, 76.2); wires tie its pins to the CAN2+ (y=83.82) and CAN2- (y=88.9) rails\"},{\"path\":\"work/geometry/geometry.json\",\"locator\":\"dnp_refs includes R36, R37; footprint R36 dnp:true, pad 1 net /CAN2+, pad 2 net /CAN2- at (175.014, 142.129)\"},{\"path\":\"inputs/project/README.md\",\"locator\":\"Inputs: 'Dual wideband O2 sensor controllers ... connected internally to CAN bus #2'\"}],\"reasoning\":\"The DNP state is clearly deliberate ('n.p.' annotation), which usually indicates termination is expected elsewhere - plausibly CAN2 is also exposed externally ('Dual CAN') and terminated in the harness, or the mck1117 wideband modules carry their own termination option. But the review scope explicitly targets internal dual-wideband CAN termination, and nothing in the packet verifies any populated termination on this bus. Classified as a concern rather than a defect because module/harness-side termination cannot be ruled out from the supplied data; major because an unterminated bus would disable both wideband controllers, a headline feature.\"},{\"id\":\"F4\",\"title\":\"Brain-module connector J2 footprint on board differs from footprint declared by its schematic symbol\",\"location\":\"Footprint J2 at (136.566, 99.212) mm\",\"condition\":\"DRC parity reports J2 uses 'Simon:Polygonus-With-USB-SWD' while the symbol specifies 'fome_modules:polygonus', plus a BOM-exclusion attribute mismatch on the same footprint.\",\"mechanism\":\"If the substitution is not a verified pin-compatible variant, any pad numbering or position difference between the two footprints would mis-route the 100+ module signals (the board's central interface). The 'Simon' library is also absent from the tool configuration, so the substituted footprint could not be checked against any library copy.\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"assessment\":\"concern\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"work/drc/drc.json\",\"locator\":\"schematic_parity: footprint_symbol_mismatch, 'Simon:Polygonus-With-USB-SWD doesn't match footprint given by symbol (fome_modules:polygonus)', Footprint J2 uuid f447e585-df78-4239-b8cb-4653b3837bb1\"}],\"reasoning\":\"The name suggests a deliberate variant adding USB/SWD access, and the saved board reports 0 unconnected items, so the nets as saved are self-consistent. However, pin-map equivalence to the symbol-declared footprint is unverified and unverifiable from the packet (library missing from configuration). Minor concern: likely intentional, but it should be reconciled in the schematic to restore parity integrity.\"},{\"id\":\"F5\",\"title\":\"Widespread library drift: 106 footprints mismatch library copies and board-local 'Simon' library absent from configuration (9 items)\",\"location\":\"Board-wide (C/R/LED/connector footprints; P1, P3, P5, P6, J1, J4 and others reference missing 'Simon' library)\",\"condition\":\"DRC reports 106 lib_footprint_mismatch violations (footprints differ from their library copies) and 9 lib_footprint_issues ('configuration does not include the footprint library Simon').\",\"mechanism\":\"Saved copper cannot be faithfully regenerated or audited against libraries; a future footprint update-from-library would silently change pad geometry across the board, and the 'Simon' footprints (including the main module connector and power pads) have no library reference at all for verification.\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"assessment\":\"concern\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"work/drc/drc.json\",\"locator\":\"violations: 106x type=lib_footprint_mismatch (e.g. C25 uuid 0070999b, R35 uuid 1905dec1); 9x type=lib_footprint_issues (e.g. P1 uuid 1646febd, J1 uuid 93ba26da, J4 uuid a7443703)\"}],\"reasoning\":\"These are warning-class native findings with no direct electrical consequence in the saved artifact, but they undermine reproducibility and future-maintenance safety of the board data. Concern (not defect) because the saved geometry itself is checked as-is and mismatches may reflect intentional local edits.\"},{\"id\":\"F6\",\"title\":\"Hierarchical label CAN_RX shaped 'input' while driven by transceiver RXD output on the CAN2 sheet\",\"location\":\"inputs/project/wbo-can-trans.kicad_sch, hierarchical label CAN_RX at (204.47, 83.82)\",\"condition\":\"The CAN_RX hierarchical label has shape 'input' (signal entering the sheet) but is wired to U20/U21 pin 4 (RXD, an output pin) inside the sheet; CAN_TX is also shape 'input'.\",\"mechanism\":\"Direction-shape mismatch on hierarchical labels is exactly the class of issue ERC flags (output pin driving an input-shaped sheet port); with ERC unable to run (F1), this latent warning is unverified. It does not alter the netlist, only connectivity-intent documentation and ERC cleanliness.\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"assessment\":\"concern\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"inputs/project/wbo-can-trans.kicad_sch\",\"locator\":\"hierarchical_label 'CAN_RX' uuid 0cfcbd19 (shape input) at (204.47, 83.82); wire (179.07, 83.82)-(204.47, 83.82) to U20 RXD pin 4 (pin type output, symbol TJA1051T-3 mirrored at 166.37, 86.36)\"}],\"reasoning\":\"Verified by tracing the sheet wiring: the RXD output reaches the input-shaped port directly. Netlist connectivity is unaffected (labels connect by name regardless of shape), so this is hygiene/ERC debt rather than an electrical fault; flagged because ERC coverage is currently zero and this would otherwise be caught there.\"},{\"id\":\"F7\",\"title\":\"14 silkscreen-clipped-by-solder-mask violations around connector legends\",\"location\":\"F.Silkscreen circles/rectangles of J6-J12, U2 overlapping PTH/SMD pads of J2 and C33 (e.g. (112.075, 56.315), (80.868, 137.564))\",\"condition\":\"Native DRC reports 14 silk_over_copper warnings where silkscreen graphics fall on mask-opened pad areas.\",\"mechanism\":\"Silkscreen over exposed pads is clipped at fabrication, degrading legend legibility; no electrical effect.\",\"severity\":\"info\",\"assessment\":\"defect\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"work/drc/drc.json\",\"locator\":\"violations: 14x type=silk_over_copper (e.g. Circle of J12 on F.Silkscreen vs PTH pad 104 [/EXT_SPI_SCK] of J2, uuid cb75ea42; Rectangle of U2 vs Pad 2 [/CAN2+] of C33, uuid 2995fbe4)\"}],\"reasoning\":\"Confirmed native violations in the saved artifact, hence a defect, but purely cosmetic: fabricators auto-clip silk from mask openings. Recorded at info severity for completeness of the native-rule coverage claim.\"}]}","structured_output":{"schema":"agent-ee.review/1","candidate_id":"693f8163ce687e039a86a686decde90440b8c14b5ae3b38c294486b2f1e4fb44","run_id":"c6cb3775-cb6c-446f-acaa-f3eb7229b643","packet_sha256":"2f16df3dacf72f02af6230e7ed9761372c19b736602edfe3e470ab96942af3c2","role":"physical","coverage":["Full read of inputs/project/wbo-can-trans.kicad_sch: transceiver supplies (VCC=+5V, VIO=+3.3V, S=GND), ESD protection (NUP2105L), filter caps, DNP 120R termination, hierarchical label shapes, wiring topology","inputs/project/README.md feature claims cross-checked against CAN2 implementation (internal dual-wideband on CAN bus #2)","work/drc/drc.json (supplied 100000-byte prefix): all schematic_parity items (114) including 15 extra_footprint and the J2 footprint substitution; silk_over_copper and lib_footprint_mismatch/lib_footprint_issues violations as included","DRC check record details: violation counts by severity (error: 13) and by type (padstack 5, annular_width 5, starved_thermal 3), 0 unconnected items","work/geometry/geometry.json 