 the existence and classification of the errors is directly evidenced by the native run."},{"id":"F3","title":"Internal dual-wideband CAN2 bus has zero populated 120R termination on the base board (both termination resistors DNP)","location":"wbo-can-trans sheet instances (R36/R37, 120R 1206 across CAN2+/CAN2-); board R36 at (175.01, 142.13) mm and R37 at (81.62, 140.55) mm","condition":"Both 120R termination resistors across /CAN2+ and /CAN2- are not populated: the schematic marks R36 '(dnp yes)', '(in_bom no)' with an 'n.p.' annotation (instance references R36 and R37 across the two sheet instances), and the board geometry lists R36 and R37 in dnp_refs with footprint R36 confirmed dnp:true spanning /CAN2+ to /CAN2-. The 47pF caps (C29/C30/C33/C34) on the bus are line-to-ground filters, not termination. README states both wideband O2 controllers are connected internally to CAN bus #2.","mechanism":"A high-speed CAN bus without ~60R differential loading suffers reflections and reduced noise margin; depending on bit rate and stub lengths this ranges from elevated error frames to total arbitration failure. The internal CAN2 segment carries the two onboard f042 wideband modules (U1/U2) plus transceiver U21, so wideband lambda data - a core advertised feature - depends on this bus. As saved, correct operation relies entirely on termination located on the plug-in wideband modules or in the external harness, neither of which is evidenced anywhere in the packet.","severity":"major","assessment":"concern","evidence":[{"path":"inputs/project/wbo-can-trans.kicad_sch","locator":"symbol R36 uuid d69380f9-5487-4782-9ce9-0690df62e543: value 120, (dnp yes), (in_bom no), instances R36/R37; text 'n.p.' uuid 98ed307b at (113.03, 76.2); wires tie its pins to the CAN2+ (y=83.82) and CAN2- (y=88.9) rails"},{"path":"work/geometry/geometry.json","locator":"dnp_refs includes R36, R37; footprint R36 dnp:true, pad 1 net /CAN2+, pad 2 net /CAN2- at (175.014, 142.129)"},{"path":"inputs/project/README.md","locator":"Inputs: 'Dual wideband O2 sensor controllers ... connected internally to CAN bus #2'"}],"reasoning":"The DNP state is clearly deliberate ('n.p.' annotation), which usually indicates termination is expected elsewhere - plausibly CAN2 is also exposed externally ('Dual CAN') and terminated in the harness, or the mck1117 wideband modules carry their own termination option. But the review scope explicitly targets internal dual-wideband CAN termination, and nothing in the packet verifies any populated termination on this bus. Classified as a concern rather than a defect because module/harness-side termination cannot be ruled out from the supplied data; major because an unterminated bus would disable both wideband controllers, a headline feature."},{"id":"F4","title":"Brain-module connector J2 footprint on board differs from footprint declared by its schematic symbol","location":"Footprint J2 at (136.566, 99.212) mm","condition":"DRC parity reports J2 uses 'Simon:Polygonus-With-USB-SWD' while the symbol specifies 'fome_modules:polygonus', plus a BOM-exclusion attribute mismatch on the same footprint.","mechanism":"If the substitution is not a verified pin-compatible variant, any pad numbering or position difference between the two footprints would mis-route the 100+ module signals (the board's central interface). The 'Simon' library is also absent from the tool configuration, so the substituted footprint could not be checked against any library copy.","severity":"minor","assessment":"concern","evidence":[{"path":"work/drc/drc.json","locator":"schematic_parity: footprint_symbol_mismatch, 'Simon:Polygonus-With-USB-SWD doesn't match footprint given by symbol (fome_modules:polygonus)', Footprint J2 uuid f447e585-df78-4239-b8cb-4653b3837bb1"}],"reasoning":"The name suggests a deliberate variant adding USB/SWD access, and the saved board reports 0 unconnected items, so the nets as saved are self-consistent. However, pin-map equivalence to the symbol-declared footprint is unverified and unverifiable from the packet (library missing from configuration). Minor concern: likely intentional, but it should be reconciled in the schematic to restore parity integrity."},{"id":"F5","title":"Widespread library drift: 106 footprints mismatch library copies and board-local 'Simon' library absent from configuration (9 items)","location":"Board-wide (C/R/LED/connector footprints; P1, P3, P5, P6, J1, J4 and others reference missing 'Simon' library)","condition":"DRC reports 106 lib_footprint_mismatch violations (footprints differ from their library copies) and 9 lib_footprint_issues ('configuration does not include the footprint library Simon').","mechanism":"Saved copper cannot be faithfully regenerated or audited against libraries; a future footprint update-from-library would silently change pad geometry across the board, and the 'Simon' footprints (including the main module connector and power pads) have no library reference at all for verification.","severity":"minor","assessment":"concern","evidence":[{"path":"work/drc/drc.json","locator":"violations: 106x type=lib_footprint_mismatch (e.g. C25 uuid 0070999b, R35 uuid 1905dec1); 9x type=lib_footprint_issues (e.g. P1 uuid 1646febd, J1 uuid 93ba26da, J4 uuid a7443703)"}],"reasoning":"These are warning-class native findings with no direct electrical consequence in the saved artifact, but they undermine reproducibility and future-maintenance safety of the board data. Concern (not defect) because the saved geometry itself is checked as-is and mismatches may reflect intentional local edits."},{"id":"F6","title":"Hierarchical label CAN_RX shaped 'input' while driven by transceiver RXD output on the CAN2 sheet","location":"inputs/project/wbo-can-trans.kicad_sch, hierarchical label CAN_RX at (204.47, 83.82)","condition":"The CAN_RX hierarchical label has shape 'input' (signal entering the sheet) but is wired to U20/U21 pin 4 (RXD, an output pin) inside the sheet; CAN_TX is also shape 'input'.","mechanism":"Direction-shape mismatch on hierarchical labels is exactly the class of issue ERC flags (output pin driving an input-shaped sheet port); with ERC unable to run (F1), this latent warning is unverified. It does not alter the netlist, only connectivity-intent documentation and ERC cleanliness.","severity":"minor","assessment":"concern","evidence":[{"path":"inputs/project/wbo-can-trans.kicad_sch","locator":"hierarchical_label 'CAN_RX' uuid 0cfcbd19 (shape input) at (204.47, 83.82); wire (179.07, 83.82)-(204.47, 83.82) to U20 RXD pin 4 (pin type output, symbol TJA1051T-3 mirrored at 166.37, 86.36)"}],"reasoning":"Verified by tracing the sheet wiring: the RXD output reaches the input-shaped port directly. Netlist connectivity is unaffected (labels connect by name regardless of shape), so this is hygiene/ERC debt rather than an electrical fault; flagged because ERC coverage is currently zero and this would otherwise be caught there."},{"id":"F7","title":"14 silkscreen-clipped-by-solder-mask violations around connector legends","location":"F.Silkscreen circles/rectangles of J6-J12, U2 overlapping PTH/SMD pads of J2 and C33 (e.g. (112.075, 56.315), (80.868, 137.564))","condition":"Native DRC reports 14 silk_over_copper warnings where silkscreen graphics fall on mask-opened pad areas.","mechanism":"Silkscreen over exposed pads is clipped at fabrication, degrading legend legibility; no electrical effect.","severity":"info","assessment":"defect","evidence":[{"path":"work/drc/drc.json","locator":"violations: 14x type=silk_over_copper (e.g. Circle of J12 on F.Silkscreen vs PTH pad 104 [/EXT_SPI_SCK] of J2, uuid cb75ea42; Rectangle of U2 vs Pad 2 [/CAN2+] of C33, uuid 2995fbe4)"}],"reasoning":"Confirmed native violations in the saved artifact, hence a defect, but purely cosmetic: fabricators auto-clip silk from mask openings. Recorded at info severity for completeness of the native-rule coverage claim."}]},"ttft_ms":102695,"type":"result","duration_ms":191823,"uuid":"57b9f2f2-ea42-44e9-a145-bb73e2b7a857","ttft_stream_ms":3458,"time_to_request_ms":245,"first_content_frame_ms":3459,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
